      "difficulty": 3,
      "confidence": 4,
      "estimatedHours": 4,
      "keyLearnings": [
        "Immutable types cannot be altered once created. Any “change” results in a new object with a different identity. Numbers (int, float, complex)  Strings (str)  Tuples (tuple)  Booleans (bool)  Bytes (bytes)  Frozen sets (frozenset)",
        "Mutable types can be modified in place without changing their identity. Lists (list)  Dictionaries (dict)  Sets (set)  Byte arrays (bytearray)  Custom classes (by default)"
      ],
